{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "03NT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-cohomology}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d1261d25e6c7efd4be1512f8690ec1bd7ba4e99548c2a6a4c17ee06799cffc7d", "source_text": "Cohomology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e3f570de094c04b0b2a36663b99d6b0a86c152f65a692d10be2c97860eb0eda8", "unit_id": "tag:03NT:title"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03NT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c5f5de76eefd06f523dd014fee447a2c600216c09445ec9a7d451f0f6fe2f860", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following is the basic result that makes it possible to define cohomology\nfor abelian sheaves on sites.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:03fd63b4c788cf753030cfef023de1e5e82a5a9b0d2e12b78903fb15d67d95dc", "unit_id": "tag:03NT:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "03NT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{theorem}\n\\label{theorem-enough-injectives}\n", "suffix": "\\end{theorem}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:59637461acd468a0b668350d025a8ed8fce2200850fab0b19d1f43428fe96f40", "source_text": "The category of abelian sheaves on a site is an abelian category\nwhich has enough injectives.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:520215d277789309c51c57ac3446849f0455ba857d0bfb8db27f8bd0cf682ab3", "unit_id": "tag:03NU:statement"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03NT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-abelian-abelian}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{injectives-theorem-sheaves-injectives}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8b61bf77f5b67f02ae1f81ce4995cf9defeaad47f5c2c44816df7f17a01e78a6", "source_text": "See\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001> and\nInjectives, Theorem <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6c9a88961923cebd5632f30c041dc16fb5455fe57c2100132ee8065240ac7993", "unit_id": "tag:03NU:proof"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03NT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F} \\in \\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nH^p(U, \\mathcal{F}) :=\nR^p\\Gamma(U, \\mathcal{F}) =\nH^p(\\Gamma(U, \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet))\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{I}^\\bullet$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Gamma(U, -)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\textit{Ab}(\\mathcal{C})$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-abelian-abelian}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-section-cohomology-sheaves}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:0875021babc3ea27ef0fc7e0001aa43a3d75a5dc993310b5e279977dd686b354", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:03677ce7a8d4bff078603b7693e24676738b9e1b0f637b4d51c7c658356c7171", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nSo we can define cohomology as the right-derived functors of the\nsections functor: if <MATH_0001> and\n<MATH_0002>,\n<MATH_0003>\nwhere <MATH_0004> is an injective resolution. To do\nthis, we should check that the functor <MATH_0005> is left exact. This is\ntrue and is part of why the category <MATH_0006> is abelian,\nsee\nModules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nFor more general discussion of cohomology on sites (including the\nglobal sections functor and its right derived functors), see\nCohomology on Sites, Section <REF_0002>.\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f20d0b4dae22e31a87060e214d6c58d79f403e2f4c79d40dd98f857fde593086", "unit_id": "tag:03NT:prose-0002"}
